# Normalise line endings so the same file does not show as modified on every
# clone.  Git was warning "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on 24 files, which is
# noise that trains you to ignore warnings - and the warnings people get
# habituated to are the ones they stop reading, which is how a real one gets
# missed.
#
# * text=auto          let git detect, and record what it decided
# * the default is LF in the repository, checked out as CRLF on Windows,
#   so the files on disk stay exactly as they are now
# * the binaries below must never be line-ending translated, or they corrupt

* text=auto eol=crlf

# Source: keep LF in the repo, CRLF in the working copy on Windows.
*.py    text eol=crlf
*.js    text eol=crlf
*.css   text eol=crlf
*.html  text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf
*.txt   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.json  text eol=crlf
*.yml   text eol=crlf
*.yaml  text eol=crlf
.gitignore    text eol=crlf
.gitattributes text eol=crlf

# Never touched - these are not text, and a translated newline in a SQLite
# file or a .gdtf archive is a corrupt file rather than a diff.
*.db      binary
*.gdtf    binary
*.gdTF    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.zip     binary
*.gz      binary
web/vendor/** -text
